    {
      "p": "每当…，总…",
      "e": "'Whenever A, B always happens' — 每当 marks a recurring occasion (more formal than 每次), and 总(会/是) states the regular outcome. 例：每当想起那段日子，他总是笑着摇头。",
      "x": "每当有火箭升空，社交媒体上总会出现同一个质疑。 — Whenever a rocket lifts off, the same challenge always appears on social media."
    },
    {
      "p": "更何况",
      "e": "'What is more; let alone' — adds a further, stronger reason after an argument has already been made, pushing the conclusion harder. 例：他连简单的句子都听不懂，更何况这样的长篇报告。",
      "x": "更何况，许多今天离不开的东西，都来自航天技术的意外收获。 — What is more, many things we cannot do without today came from the unexpected spin-offs of aerospace technology."
    },
    {
      "p": "也不是没有…（双重否定）",
      "e": "A double negative that concedes a point mildly: 'it is not that there is no…', i.e. there is some. Softer and more balanced than a flat affirmative. 例：这个计划也不是没有风险，只是风险可以控制。",
      "x": "怀疑者的担忧也不是没有道理。 — The skeptics' worries are not without foundation either."
